comments.body:
**CI capacity note (07:58Z), for the owner.** Since #2192 removed the runtime mutex, runtime runs go in parallel, and the binding limit has moved to **GitHub's concurrent-job cap**: 21 runs queued and 11 in progress repo-wide. A required `check-test` waited about 9.5 minutes for a runner. #2195 (#2194's shards) cuts the wall time per run, but adds more jobs per run, so it helps only while runners are free.

**What I'm doing:**
- cancelling queued runs on heads an in-flight fix will supersede;
- arming runtime only once per PR, after the reviewer's verdict is in;
- making no label edits during runs.

**Options if you want more throughput:** a higher concurrent-job allowance on the GitHub plan, or first-party GitHub larger runners (no third-party vendors). Otherwise the 10:30Z canary.3 cut takes whatever has merged by then.

## Audit execution update — 2026-09-22

I have restarted the #34 audit from the current `master` commit rather than trusting previous audit summaries.

### Phase 0
- 0.1–0.7: baseline/spec/TASKS/CHECKLIST reconciliation is in progress.
- Important governance point confirmed: code presence is not acceptance; every item requires implementation + tests + quantitative/physical evidence + CI + final PR audit.

### Phase 1
The HDF5 foundation is present, but 1.2/1.3 are **not yet considered complete** until full reconstruction of mesh + fields + physics + numerics is demonstrated. PR #148 addresses the case + paired DAT artifact contract but explicitly does not yet claim solver-level numerical continuation.

### Phase 2 — concrete defects found
The first direct audit found a real geometry defect that was hidden by the existing one-cell tests:
- internal-face quality used the owner→face direction instead of the owner→neighbour line;
- GeometryCache used the boundary quality metric for internal faces;
- GeometryCache surface closure summed owner-oriented face vectors without reversing neighbour faces;
- cached face vectors were not canonicalized after cell centres were known.

I implemented corrections and added a deliberately reversed shared-face two-cell regression in **PR #149**.

### Phase 3 — defects confirmed
The next audit confirms:
- gradient/divergence/laplacian still rebuild geometry internally;
- a GeometryCache already exists, so the duplicate geometry paths should be removed rather than creating another geometry abstraction;
- Laplacian exposes corrected/limited schemes but current master still routes through the same orthogonal implementation;
- LIMITED interpolation still contains the previously identified placeholder/approximation and does not yet perform true multidimensional gradient reconstruction;
- matrix-free remains a skeleton.

### Next sequence
I will continue strictly in roadmap order:
1. finish/audit Phase 2 geometry/import contracts;
2. integrate the existing GeometryCache into the numerical operators and repeated physics assembly paths;
3. correct/validate interpolation and Laplacian schemes;
4. add operator-level MMS/conservation/refinement tests;
5. only then move to Phase 4 linear algebra.

No roadmap item will be marked complete merely because a corresponding class/API exists.

GUI/restart integration completed as part of the #112 closure.

Merged:
- #148: HDF5 + paired DAT persistence and validation;
- #161: canonical case.cfdx.h5 -> case.dat pairing;
- #166: ExecutionConfig.restart_option and GUI propagation of the validated DAT to the solver command.

The GUI now refuses to silently ignore a loaded DAT when restart support is disabled. Numerical interpretation and continuation validation remain solver responsibilities; the application layer validates artifact pairing and constructs the restart launch contract.

### Phase 4.1 — new concrete finding and PR #254

The sparse foundation audit found a real correctness defect in the pre-existing CSR builder: `SparseMatrix::push_back()` incremented row offsets by row, but stored values in insertion order. The Laplacian assembler can emit rows in arbitrary order, so the resulting CSR ranges could associate coefficients with the wrong rows while `is_consistent()` still returned true.

PR #254 fixes this by staging assembly entries, canonicalizing them to CSR in `finalize()`, preserving legitimate duplicate coefficients, and hardening finite/index/order invariants. It also adds focused regression tests.

**Status:** 4.1 remains 🟡 until PR #254 is CI-green and audited/merged.

### 4.7 AMG — audit started

The current `MatrixFreeVcyclePreconditioner` is explicitly an **agglomerated matrix-free V-cycle foundation**, not yet a production AMG implementation:
- pair/connectivity aggregation exists;
- fine-level smoothing exists;
- restriction/prolongation are implicit through aggregation;
- coarse correction currently uses an aggregated **diagonal approximation**, not a Galerkin coarse operator;
- only one coarse level is built;
- setup currently does not require `A.is_consistent()`;
- strength/aggregation needs explicit finite/diagonal/sign/CFD-matrix robustness contracts;
- residual-reduction validation exists, but convergence/conditioning coverage must be expanded before 4.7 can be marked complete.

I will keep 4.7 open and separate this foundation from a real multilevel AMG implementation.

Phase 4.7 update — PR #255 was audited and strengthened.

Completed on the branch:
- multilevel Galerkin AMG hierarchy remains in place;
- 1D Poisson (32) and 2D Poisson (8x8) quantitative residual checks;
- duplicate-diagonal regression for FVM-style assembly;
- strongly anisotropic diffusion regression (16x16, anisotropy 1000:1);
- repeated four V-cycle residual-reduction check;
- representative cell-centred FVM diffusion assembly with directional coefficients.

Also fixed the test's CSR row ordering after adding the anisotropic reaction term. Current head: c6c29fb512f360716a73c4623b50cb966a7f24f6, 0 commits behind master.

Fresh CFDX CI, build/tests and validation workflows are running. No merge is being done before those checks complete.

### 2026-09-23 — Phase 1 HDF5 integrity follow-up

PR #305 was audited and **closed without merge** because its branch was stale/corrupted relative to current master: it showed ~2,205 changed files, including build artifacts and massive deletions, with no current-head CI. It was not used as roadmap evidence.

A clean replacement **PR #306** was created directly from current master.

PR #306 scope:
- enforce required HDF5 format/schema metadata on read;
- reject unsupported format/schema versions;
- recompute and verify the persisted topology hash;
- recompute and verify the persisted mesh hash before reconstruction;
- add schema-version, topology-hash, mesh-hash and missing-metadata corruption regressions.

**Phase 1 status:** 1.5/1.6/1.9 remain 🟡 PARTIAL until #306 is green, audited and merged; this PR deliberately does not claim the entire Phase 1 corruption/compatibility matrix.

### Phase 3.6 — PR #323 opened

PR #323 adds the missing quantitative skew/non-orthogonal campaign identified in the Phase 3 audit.

Coverage:
- controlled skew sweep: 0, 0.05, 0.10, 0.20, 0.30, 0.40;
- orthogonal vs corrected Laplacian response;
- finite-value checks;
- volume-integrated internal-face conservation gate at 1e-12;
- explicit zero-skew equivalence and non-zero-skew correction checks;
- CMake registration and dedicated validation documentation.

Scope is intentionally explicit: this does not implement LIMITED, and it does not claim the broader full-mesh MMS/refinement matrix is complete.

**Status: 🟡 pending CI + final audit + merge.**

### 2026-09-23 — Phase 5 consolidated implementation

PR #326 — **open / CI in progress**: `feat(mpi): complete Phase 5 distributed execution and restart`.

This PR consolidates the remaining Phase-5 work into one integration:
- distributed local cell ownership with persistent global IDs;
- exact distributed ownership validation without replicating the full ID set on every rank;
- local-field MPI halo exchange;
- collective Parallel HDF5 checkpoint write/read;
- rank/order-independent restart by persistent global cell ID;
- deterministic MPI reduction exercised in the distributed regression;
- 2-rank executable regression and CTest registration;
- explicit `CFDX_ENABLE_PARALLEL_HDF5` configuration contract.

The PR deliberately does **not** claim that the physics/Krylov solver implementations themselves are already distributed; their APIs remain serial. The new layer is the Phase-5 data/execution contract intended for subsequent solver integration.

Required CI must be green before merge.

## Phase 6 — runtime/GPU acceptance update

PR #350 has been **merged** into `master` (squash commit `eaedbe64d61d129af3df8deb3e812e2aee998f9c`).

### Integrated scope
- CPU/GPU execution-policy contracts and explicit GPU fail-fast behavior;
- memory-planner and memory-budget acceptance checks;
- real CUDA gradient execution path when CUDA hardware is available;
- pinned staging buffers retained until stream synchronization;
- asynchronous H2D/D2H transfer handling;
